code: K0037
title: Assert Outside Test
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, assert, test, unit-testing, scope]
description: "'assert' is only allowed directly inside a 'test' block"
---

The `assert` statement is only valid directly inside the top-level body of a `test "..." { ... }` block. It cannot appear at the top level of a file, inside regular functions, or nested inside inner `if`, `match`, or `for` blocks.

## Example

This error occurs when `assert` is used inside a regular `fn` or nested inside a control-flow block within a `test`:

```kura
fn check(x: Int): Int => {
  assert(x > 0)
  x
}

test "nested assert" {
  if true {
    assert(1 == 1)
  } else {
    None
  }
}
```

## Solution

Move `assert` calls directly into a `test` block body (using `static-assert` if you need a compile-time invariant outside tests):

```kura
test "positive check" {
  let x = 5
  assert(x > 0)
}
```
